WHY WE BOTHER SAYING IT

Acuario is a research project. It was built to advance open security research
and to be studied, learned from, and improved - not to be sold. We would
rather say what we hope for and leave it to your judgement than pretend the
licence says something it does not.

WHAT WE HOPE YOU WILL DO

  - Use Acuario for research, education, internal security work, and the
    improvement of software security generally, rather than as the basis of
    a commercial product sold to others.

  - Give a different name to any substantially modified version, so that
    security findings produced by your version are not mistaken for findings
    produced by ours.

  - Do not describe your work as endorsed, certified, accredited, or approved
    by DSCI unless DSCI has actually said so.

  - Cite the project if it contributes to published work.

  - Send fixes and improvements upstream if you are willing. This is the
    whole reason the project is public.

The naming request matters more than the others, and not for commercial
reasons. Acuario produces security findings that people act on. A modified
version returning different results under the same name misleads its users
about who stands behind those results. That is a question of honest
provenance, and it is the one item we would genuinely urge you to respect
even if you ignore the rest.

WHAT WE ARE NOT DOING

We are not registering trademarks, tracking copies, monitoring forks, or
policing compliance beyond the licence itself. We will not pursue anyone for
declining any of the above. This is a research project run by people with
other work to do.

